2024-03-27T19:57:42 --------------------------
2024-03-27T19:57:42 |Hi Andrew,
2024-03-27T19:57:42 |
2024-03-27T19:57:42 |Andrew Fresh wrote on Fri, May 03, 2019 at 06:24:16PM -0700:
2024-03-27T19:57:42 |
2024-03-27T19:57:42 |> I committed this after moving the waitpid down a few lines, after the
2024-03-27T19:57:42 |> last read from the filehandle.
2024-03-27T19:57:42 |
2024-03-27T19:57:42 |Oops. Sorry for missing that, and thanks for committing it,
2024-03-27T19:57:42 |and for catching that additional issue.
2024-03-27T19:57:42 |
2024-03-27T19:57:42 |> I will say that `perldoc -oterm unicook` looks a lot better with the
2024-03-27T19:57:42 |> right fonts and LC_CTYPE=en_US.UTF-8 than the output from -oman, but it
2024-03-27T19:57:42 |> looks a lot worse with LC_CTYPE=C so probably -oman is a better default.
2024-03-27T19:57:42 |
2024-03-27T19:57:42 |Specifically,
2024-03-27T19:57:42 |
2024-03-27T19:57:42 | LC_CTYPE=en_US.UTF-8 LESS=-R perldoc -oterm # produces UTF-8 (fine)
2024-03-27T19:57:42 | LC_CTYPE=en_US.UTF-8 perldoc -oman # produces UTF-8 (fine)
2024-03-27T19:57:42 | # with the patch below
2024-03-27T19:57:42 |
2024-03-27T19:57:42 | LC_CTYPE=C LESS=-R perldoc -oterm unicook # produces UTF-8 (bad)
2024-03-27T19:57:42 | LC_CTYPE=C perldoc -oman unicook # produces ASCII (good)
2024-03-27T19:57:42 |
2024-03-27T19:57:42 |So -oterm is definitely a bad default, and fixing it may be a waste
2024-03-27T19:57:42 |of time. I see no point in maintaining alternative output modes that
2024-03-27T19:57:42 |provide little to no benefit.
2024-03-27T19:57:42 |
2024-03-27T19:57:42 |> Perhaps I can figure out how to get ToMan to do the right thing in the
2024-03-27T19:57:42 |> right locale someday.
2024-03-27T19:57:42 |
2024-03-27T19:57:42 |The first chunk in the patch below seems to be all that is needed.
2024-03-27T19:57:42 |
2024-03-27T19:57:42 |IIRC, we already do a similar thing in pod2man(1).
2024-03-27T19:57:42 |
2024-03-27T19:57:42 |Of course, both chunks can be OK'ed / objected to independently,
2024-03-27T19:57:42 |they are completely independent of each other. I'm merely leaving
2024-03-27T19:57:42 |both in place such that they don't get forgotten.
2024-03-27T19:57:42 |
2024-03-27T19:57:42 |Yours,
2024-03-27T19:57:43 | Ingo
2024-03-27T19:57:43 |
